 you don't clean yourself up you might  not be seeing me around for it  that'll kick your neck really quick me I  started with walking I mean my like I  said I'd always been an athlete and  always you know played basketball on the  road did all kinds of things but when I  came to it when it came to having a sort  of a focused workout the first thing I  started to do is walk and that led to  running and then running led to CrossFit  and lifting weights without even  noticing an unknown notice I'd do a lot  of things now in my show that that come  directly from some of the workouts that  I did certainly some of the bodyweight  stuff and sort of the mobility stuff  that I do with Roger who's the guy's  trained me for five or six years now  the stuff that I do with him it shows up  on stage and also just singing just a my  singing my condition the condition that  I think I've seen better now than I ever  have and I think that's a big part of  the workouts in the exercise and the  fitness um it gives me all kinds of  latitude to do the things that I want to  do on stage and not worry so much about  having to catch my breath and sing the  song
 

